  "goodToKnow": "Netto means net, i.e. after deductions: Ich verdiene 2.800 Euro netto, which is what lands in your account after tax and social contributions. The opposite is brutto (gross). On packaging, Nettogewicht is the weight of the contents without packaging. Nettopreis in business means the price before VAT (Mehrwertsteuer). Netto comes from Italian, like many financial terms: brutto, netto, Konto, Skonto."
